Description: Google Tasks counter and window for the XFCE panel
 Shows the number of open Google Tasks in the XFCE panel through the
 Generic Monitor (genmon) plugin. One click on the item opens a popup
 with the open tasks, a check button for each one and a quick-add
 field. Two clicks open a GTK window with the task lists, the tasks and
 a detail pane to change title, notes, due date and list.
 .
 The tasks stay in the panel. After the first sign-in you do not open
 the Google Tasks web page again.
 .
 After install: put your OAuth client_secret.json in
 ~/.config/gtasks-panel/, run "gtasks-panel --auth", then
 "gtasks-panel --install-panel".

